---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';

const countries = [
  { name: 'Kenya', records: 1320, farmers: 18232 },
  { name: 'Uganda', records: 2377, farmers: 4929 },
].map((c) => ({ ...c, share: (c.records / c.farmers) * 100 }));
---

<CaseStudy
  slug="nest-coverage"
  facts={[
    ['Where', 'Trees for the Future, Kenya and Uganda'],
    ['Method', 'Unique monitoring records against registered farmers, over matched collection windows'],
    ['Audience', 'Programme leadership'],
  ]}
>
  <section class="split">
    <h2 class="label">Problem</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        NEST is one of the programme's field monitoring forms. Kenya and Uganda were returning very different numbers
        of records, and leadership read the gap as a matter of geography and timing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split">
    <h2 class="label">What I did</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I counted unique records per farmer in each country, set them against the number of registered farmers, and
        compared collection windows of similar length. I also cross-referenced the records with the spatial extent of
        the farms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo" aria-labelledby="bars-h">
    <div class="demo-head">
      <h2 class="label" id="bars-h">NEST coverage of registered farmers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-body bars">
      {
        countries.map((c) => (
          <div class="row">
            <span>{c.name}</span>
            <div class="track">
              <div class="bar" style={`width:${c.share.toFixed(1)}%`} />
            </div>
            <b>{c.share.toFixed(1)}%</b>
            <span class="label">
              {c.records.toLocaleString('en')} of {c.farmers.toLocaleString('en')} farmers
            </span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="demo-foot label">Reported programme figures, not generated data.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="split">
    <h2 class="label">Result</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Kenya had 1,320 unique records from 18,232 registered farmers, which is 7.2%. Uganda had 2,377 from 4,929,
        which is 48.2%. The windows were similar, so elapsed time could not account for a gap that size.
      </p>
      <p>
        I put the case to leadership that the difference came from how teams collected and reported. That pointed the
        corrective action at work planning and reporting discipline.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also rebuilt the NEST reporting workbook so one file adapts to each country, handles repeat visits and
        carries notes on field problems.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split">
    <h2 class="label">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Break coverage down by project unit and by field officer, to see where the missing records are concentrated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseStudy>

<style>
  .bars {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5rem minmax(0, 1fr) 4.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem 1rem;
  }

  .track {
    border-left: 1px solid var(--muted);
  }

  .bar {
    height: 2.25rem;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .row b {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-family: var(--display);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .row .label {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
  }
</style>
